<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Tai Yung defaults on notes.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Tai Yung defaults on notes.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Tai Yung Paper Board Manufacturing Co Ltd has defaulted on payments of 1.5 billion won worth of promissory notes, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The Korea Stock Exchange said on Wednesday that the trading in the stock would be halted from Wednesday morning.  </p>
<p>&quot;We failed to settle the payments of 1.5 billion won in total,&quot; said the official.</p>
<p>Tai Yung was last traded at 23,000 won.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
